directory as owner to do what I need to get done.

So...  if a shell script is setup as r-sr-xr-x what can anyone do to modify
the script or coerce it into doing something other than it's intended purpose?

Is it somehow possible to execute the shell script and then snare the euid
directly from the spawned process and use it further?  This is the only
(serious) threat I could see.

